Busybox TODO

Stuff that needs to be done.

Applet parity roadmap:
  * Complete POSIX audit against Single Unix Specification V3
  * sed: stream editor pattern matching and in-place editing
  * awk: pattern-directed scanning and processing language
  * tar: ustar/pax archive format reading and writing
  * find: expression tree traversal with -exec and prune
  * ash: POSIX shell parsing, job control, signals, parameter expansion
  * mount / umount: Linux mount syscall wrapper with fstab parsing

Architecture and performance:
  * Further size optimizations for embedded targets
  * Direct zero-copy splicing on Linux kernels via splice/tee syscalls
  * Strict memory safety without sacrificing byte-level compatibility
